      "locator": "Section 7.1.3.1, report p.184",
      "scope": "Primary NIST guidance states the simple convection relation Qc=h*As*(Ts-Tf), notes typical fire-compartment h values of about 10 to 30 W/(m2 K), and treats convection plus radiation as the surface boundary for conduction. V11K reverses the sign to report heat into the coupon."
    },
    {
